<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="047" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Foreign-environment readability 403 logs at Warning (or skips with a cooldown); own environment stays fail-closed (FR-31 c, #2578)</title>
    <phase>4 Access, sign-in, carry-overs, Teams</phase>
    <gate>after 038 (P3 deploy)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tag bff-api; modifies an existing scheduled job (.cs) under Services/</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single existing job with exact anchors; brownfield behaviour needs careful reasoning, hence xhigh effort</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>038</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, job, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Stop the identity-link reconciliation job raising an App Insights Error every 5 minutes when a FOREIGN registered environment (dev: spaarke-acme) refuses the BFF's readability proof with a membership 403: log it at Warning, or skip that environment with a cooldown. The BFF's own environment must stay exactly as fail-closed and as loud as today.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in the BFF's IdentityLinkReconciliationJob (ADR-036 IScheduledJob) and the secured-column readability proof.</role>
  <goal>A foreign environment's membership-403 probe failure produces no Error-level telemetry (Warning, or a cooldown skip); every other probe failure, and every own-environment failure, behaves as before; tests prove both.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Evidence (design.md §7.2, uac-r2 gate on 20669df6a9, 2026-11-06): each fault pairs with `[ID-LINK-RECON] https://spaarke-acme.crm.dynamics.com: binding column Failed … environment aborted before any decision`. The WhoAmI read answers 403 0x80072560 "not a member of the organization". Flow: `ExecuteAsync` reconciles the own environment (IdentityLinkReconciliationJob.cs:249) then `ReconcileProvisioningTargetsAsync` (:405-470), which loops `ProvisioningTargetUrls` (:200-227; never the own environment, by `RegistrationDataverseService.IsSameEnvironment`) and calls the SAME `ReconcileEnvironmentAsync` (:373-398). That method logs `LogError` and aborts when `ProbeBindingReadabilityAsync` returns Masked or Failed (:376-386). The probe (ContactIdentityStore.cs:1777-1794) returns Failed when the proof faults; the proof's WhoAmI read is `WebApiColumnReadPermissionSource.ReadOwnUserIdAsync` (:2295) via `ReadProofAsync` (:2316), and SecuredColumnReadProof.cs logs the fault at Warning (:169-174). `BindingReadability` (ContactIdentityStore.cs:179) does not say WHY it failed. The data side (application user / registry row) is task 046.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/IdentityLinkReconciliationJob.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ContactIdentityStore.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/SecuredColumnReadProof.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/DataverseEnvironmentService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/IdentityBinding/IdentityLinkReconciliationTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/ExternalAccess/IdentityLinkReconciliationRegistryTargetsTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-047-notes.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="038" status="pending">P3 deployed and E2E-proved (phase-deploy convention)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-31 c">The change applies only to provisioning-target (foreign) environments reconciled from ReconcileProvisioningTargetsAsync. The own-environment call (:249) keeps LogError and abort on Masked or Failed, unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (fail closed)">A foreign environment whose probe fails is still aborted before any decision (`ProbeBlocked`); only the log level (or a cooldown skip) changes. Masking (BindingReadability.Masked) on a foreign environment stays an Error — it is a real configuration fault, not a membership refusal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-31 c">Prefer Warning over a cooldown: a cooldown needs per-environment state across runs; if chosen, it uses the injected TimeProvider, lives in the job instance, and the run report still records the environment as skipped.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-052 / ADR-036">No new background work, timer, hosted service or schedule; this edits the existing IScheduledJob only. No new DI registration, interface or package (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Log lines name the environment URL and codes only — no tenant, oid, UPN, email or token; never the response body.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions">Placement Justification in the PR (.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); publish-size delta against a fresh master build, at or under 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; tests with this Services/ change; /conflict-check before the PR (the job is shared with unified-access-control-r2). Never deploy the dev BFF directly — request via uac-r2 (docs/procedures/dev-bff-deploy-coordination.md).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests under KEEP paths (extend IdentityLinkReconciliationTests.cs under tests/integration/auth/**); time via FakeTimeProvider; no Stopwatch/Task.Delay/DateTime.UtcNow.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/background-workers.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/scheduled-jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-052-workload-placement.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Own vs foreign environment" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/IdentityLinkReconciliationJob.cs">`ProvisioningTargetUrls` (:200-227) already excludes the own environment by `IsSameEnvironment`; pass "foreign" into the shared method rather than re-deriving it from a URL.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">List every Error-level log and exception telemetry one acme pass emits today (job line :382, the proof's Warning-with-exception, the GetAsync warning); record which reach App Insights as Error.</step>
    <step order="2">Decide how a membership 403 is told apart from other probe failures (a reason on the proof outcome, or the probe result), with the smallest change; record the design and why in the notes.</step>
    <step order="3">Make ReconcileEnvironmentAsync aware of own vs foreign (a parameter from its two callers); on a foreign membership-403 log Warning (or apply the cooldown) and keep the abort and the run report fields.</step>
    <step order="4">Tests: foreign membership 403 → no Error-level log, environment aborted, report records it; own-environment Failed and Masked → Error and abort exactly as before (must-not-fire); foreign Masked → still Error.</step>
    <step order="5">Seeding proof: make the own-environment path take the foreign branch, confirm the own-environment test fails, restore; record it.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` and the affected tests (re-run timeouts in isolation); measure publish size.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-047-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a membership 403 cannot be told apart from other probe faults without changing the shared SecuredColumnReadProof contract used by the BFF's own environment, STOP and ask UAC before changing it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any change would let a foreign environment be reconciled (decisions or writes) after a failed probe, STOP — the abort is the fail-closed control.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ExternalAccess/IdentityLinkReconciliationJob.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/IdentityBinding/IdentityLinkReconciliationTests.cs (extended)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-047-notes.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a foreign environment whose readability proof fails with a membership 403, the run emits no Error-level log for it (Warning, or a cooldown skip recorded in the report) and makes no decision or write there.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Must-not-fire: the own environment's Failed and Masked probes still log Error and abort exactly as before (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a foreign environment that is Masked, or fails for a reason other than membership, still logs Error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new background service, timer, DI registration, interface or package.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No log line added or changed carries a tenant, oid, UPN, email, token or response body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The seeding proof is recorded; UAC's review is recorded in the notes and the PR (FR-31).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; publish size at or under 60 MB with the delta against a fresh master build; no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check run; affected tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the must-not-fire and negative cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-31 (c); issue #2578 (#2163 closed as its duplicate). The live acceptance ("0 acme faults in 30 minutes, or logged at Warning") is checked in task 058's gate after 046's data fix and this deploy. plan.md's critical path lists 046 → 047; the task table makes 047 independent (deps 038) because the code change does not need the data fix — run 046's checks first if both are open.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
